  "releaseNotes": "======================================================\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n Version 10.0.0\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n======================================================\n\n\n==========================================\n Bugfixes\n==========================================\n- Correct request URI and endpoint path handling, including slashes and trailing endpoint name in HealthServiceRestClient (#305)\n\n\n==========================================\nNew Features\n==========================================\n- Support externally managed HttpClient instances and custom request handler chains (#305)\n    ○ Refactor REST-client abstractions, service interfaces, and configuration handling\n    ○ RestClient class represents the default implementation for desktop scenarios, using an internal HttpClient as before\n    ○ HttpClientRestClient class allows providing an externally managed and configured HttpClient, e.g. for browser scenarios\n    ○ For the simple usage of the Data/RawDataServiceRestClients, no breaking changes should surface for desktop clients\n    ○ For scenarios with custom rest clients implementing our interfaces, changes may be necessary\n- Remove browser/WASM platform support from RestClient class (#307)\n    ○ Direct consequence of #305\n    ○ In browser scenarios, use HttpClientRestClient and inject an HttpClient instance directly to the service REST clients\n- Add a standalone caching extension with ICachingHandlerFactory and CacheCow-based filesystem stores (#308)\n    ○ Introduce ICachingHandlerFactory to abstract caching handler creation and move CacheCow-based caching to new Api.Rest.Caching project\n    ○ Update RestClient and builder to use the new factory, removing direct CacheCow dependencies\n    ○ Reduces overhead in browser scenarios, since caching is handled by the browser itself\n- Add several new keys to WellKnownKeys (#303 and #309)\n    ○ Add well-known keys for part distribution analysis mode\n    ○ Add well-known keys for measurement callback URI and callback description",
